@anon.a2b023d1a4e2834952d16152dce23780.855 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [792 x i8] }> <{ [792 x i8] c"Create an [Oklab](https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/) color.\0A\0AThis color space is well suited for the following use cases:\0A- Color manipulation such as saturating while keeping perceived hue\0A- Creating grayscale images with uniform perceived lightness\0A- Creating smooth and uniform color transition and gradients\0A\0AA linear Oklab color is represented internally by an array of four\0Acomponents:\0A- lightness ([`ratio`])\0A- a ([`float`] or [`ratio`].\0A  Ratios are relative to `{0.4}`; meaning `{50%}` is equal to `{0.2}`)\0A- b ([`float`] or [`ratio`].\0A  Ratios are relative to `{0.4}`; meaning `{50%}` is equal to `{0.2}`)\0A- alpha ([`ratio`])\0A\0AThese components are also available using the\0A[`components`]($color.components) method.\0A\0A```example\0A#square(\0A  fill: oklab(27%, 20%, -3%, 50%)\0A)\0A```" }>, align 1
